From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the GPU sandbox lets Gentoo's Mesa load

NickelOS Unified has one Mesa, Gentoo's, for Chrome and Linux apps. The
GPU sandbox's file lists name Google's Mesa build: libgallium_dri.so,
libglapi.so.0, the drivers in dri/. Gentoo's core library carries its
version (libgallium-26.1.8.so), its drivers load through
dri/libdril_dri.so, it links LLVM from /usr/lib/llvm/<slot>/ and the X11,
xcb and Wayland client libraries, and libdrm follows /sys/dev/char into
/sys/devices for the GPU's PCI ids. With gpu_sandbox_start_early (Intel
and AMD boards, for Mesa's threads) the driver loads inside the sandbox:
EGL got no display, the GPU process exited, and Chrome, with no software
compositing, quit before the login screen (the Intel test PC, 2026-10-20).
On AMD, Intel, NVIDIA and VirtIO GPUs the sandbox now also reads, and only
reads, the library directories, the loader's cache, /sys/devices and
Mesa's driver settings.

diff --git a/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc b/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
index c41e683d837f1..2c96f4b4c8d05 100644
--- a/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+++ b/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
@@ -254,6 +254,29 @@ void AddDrmGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
   }
 }
 
+// NickelOS: Gentoo's Mesa, for Chrome and Linux apps alike (one Mesa), is
+// not Google's build these lists name: its core library carries its version
+// (libgallium-26.1.8.so), its drivers load through dri/libdril_dri.so, it
+// links LLVM from /usr/lib/llvm/<slot>/ and the X11, xcb and Wayland client
+// libraries, and libdrm follows the GPU's /sys/dev/char link into
+// /sys/devices for its PCI ids. With the sandbox started early
+// (gpu_sandbox_start_early, for Mesa's threads) all of it is opened from
+// inside the sandbox, so Chrome had no GPU and no login screen on Intel and
+// AMD (2026-10-20): the libraries' directories, the loader's cache, those
+// sysfs trees and Mesa's driver settings, read-only.
+void AddNickelMesaPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
+  static const char* const kReadOnlyRecursive[] = {
+      "/usr/lib64/", "/usr/lib/llvm/", "/sys/devices/", "/usr/share/drirc.d/",
+      "/usr/share/libdrm/"};
+  for (const char* dir : kReadOnlyRecursive) {
+    permissions->push_back(BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnlyRecursive(dir));
+  }
+  static const char* const kReadOnly[] = {"/etc/ld.so.cache", "/etc/drirc"};
+  for (const char* item : kReadOnly) {
+    permissions->push_back(BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnly(item));
+  }
+}
+
 void AddAmdGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
   static const char* const kReadOnlyList[] = {
       "/etc/ld.so.cache",
@@ -274,6 +297,7 @@ void AddAmdGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
   for (const char* item : kReadOnlyList)
     permissions->push_back(BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnly(item));
 
+  AddNickelMesaPermissions(permissions);
   AddDrmGpuPermissions(permissions);
 
   // NOTE: control nodes are probably not required:
@@ -333,6 +357,7 @@ void AddNvidiaGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
   permissions->push_back(
       BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnlyRecursive("/proc/driver/nvidia/"));
 
+  AddNickelMesaPermissions(permissions);
   AddDrmGpuPermissions(permissions);
 }
 
@@ -357,6 +382,7 @@ void AddIntelGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
   for (const char* item : kReadOnlyList)
     permissions->push_back(BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnly(item));
 
+  AddNickelMesaPermissions(permissions);
   AddDrmGpuPermissions(permissions);
 }
 
@@ -401,6 +427,7 @@ void AddVirtIOGpuPermissions(std::vector<BrokerFilePermission>* permissions) {
     permissions->push_back(BrokerFilePermission::ReadOnlyRecursive(path + "/"));
   }
 
+  AddNickelMesaPermissions(permissions);
   AddDrmGpuPermissions(permissions);
 }
 
